# Per-deployment inputs and state. None of these belong in the repository: backend.hcl and
# terraform.tfvars name one account's resources, and a state file is a credential-adjacent artifact
# even when this module set keeps secret material out of it.
backend.hcl
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/

# The dependency lock file is normally committed for a root module, and it is not committed here for
# one specific reason: the only lock this repository has produced was generated on darwin_arm64 and
# records hashes for that platform alone, so committing it would break `terraform init` for anyone on
# Linux. Whoever runs the first real apply should generate a multi-platform lock
# (`terraform providers lock -platform=linux_amd64 -platform=linux_arm64 -platform=darwin_arm64`),
# commit it, and delete these six lines.
.terraform.lock.hcl
crash.log
